{"content":[{"c":["KIRIATHAIM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Town on the Moabite plateau, mentioned in the march of the four kings against the five (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.14.5","r":"Gen.14.5","rawR":"Gen.14.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.14.5","value":"Gen.14.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 14:5"},") where the indigenous Emim were attacked. It was taken by the Israelites from Sihon (",{"href":"?bref=Num.32.37","r":"Num.32.37","rawR":"Num.32.37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.32.37","value":"Num.32.37"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 32:37"},") and included in Reuben’s inheritance (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.13.19","r":"Josh.13.19","rawR":"Josh.13.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.13.19","value":"Josh.13.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 13:19"},"). The Moabite Stone records that Sihon fortified the place after gaining control of the plateau; in the seventh century ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," it was still under Moabite control (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.48.1,23","r":"Jer.48.1,23","rawR":"Jer.48.1,23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.48.1,23","value":"Jer.48.1,23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 48:1, 23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.25.9","r":"Ezek.25.9","rawR":"Ezek.25.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.25.9","value":"Ezek.25.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 25:9"},"). Eusebius placed it 10 Roman miles west of Medeba. Two identifications have been proposed—either Khirbet el-Qureiyeh or Qaryat el-Mukhaiyet, six miles (9.7 kilometers) northwest and three miles (4.8 kilometers) northwest of Medeba respectively."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Levitical town in Naphtali’s territory (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.76","r":"1Chr.6.76","rawR":"1Chr.6.76","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.76","value":"1Chr.6.76"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:76"},"), called Kartan in ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.32","r":"Josh.21.32","rawR":"Josh.21.32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.32","value":"Josh.21.32"}],"t":"ref","v":"Joshua 21:32"},"; the latter is probably a dialectical variant. The suggested identification is with Khirbet el-Qurieyeh, northeast of ‘Ain Ibl in southern Lebanon."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=LeviticalCities_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"LeviticalCities_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"LeviticalCities_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Levitical Cities"},"."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Kiriathaim","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 14:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.14.5","rawQueryValue":"Gen.14.5","sourceRefExact":"Gen.14.5"},{"anchorText":"Nm 32:37","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.32.37","rawQueryValue":"Num.32.37","sourceRefExact":"Num.32.37"},{"anchorText":"Jos 13:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.13.19","rawQueryValue":"Josh.13.19","sourceRefExact":"Josh.13.19"},{"anchorText":"Jer 48:1, 23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.48.1,23","rawQueryValue":"Jer.48.1,23","sourceRefExact":"Jer.48.1,23"},{"anchorText":"Ez 25:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.25.9","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.25.9","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.25.9"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:76","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.76","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.76","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.76"},{"anchorText":"Joshua 21:32","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.21.32","rawQueryValue":"Josh.21.32","sourceRefExact":"Josh.21.32"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"55a7822d8ea0788a8b0095f2dd3a91b12cb7cc0dda9c7cca0df67e6215b2008e","sourceItemName":"Kiriathaim","sourceItemOrder":94,"sourceMember":"Articles/K.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Kiriathaim","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Kiriathaim","title":"Kiriathaim","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}